course: dictionary
lesson: 8206
title: The retina: the eye's light sensor
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The retina is the thin layer at the back of the inside of your eye. It senses light and sends messages to your brain, so without it you could not see anything. «The lens in the eye works like a magnifying glass and makes a picture on the retina at the back of the eye.» Picture means the image of what you are looking at.
explain: Think of your eye as a camera. «Your eye is like a camera: the clear front and the lens bend light so it focuses in a sharp picture on the retina at the back.» The light bends first, then lands on the retina, and the retina passes the message on.
explain: The picture on the retina is upside down, but you do not see the world upside down. «The image on the retina is upside down; the brain turns it round.» Your brain does the sorting out, so the picture looks the right way up to you.
fact: The retina is the thin layer at the back of the inside of the eye.
fact: The retina senses light and sends messages to the brain.
fact: The lens bends light so it focuses on the retina.
fact: «Glasses lenses bend light so it focuses on the retina, and wearing them does not make eyes worse.»
fact: In science, rods on the retina see in dim light, and cones see colour.
exercise: «The lens in the eye makes a picture on the retina.» Where is the retina? | On the nose | In the ear | At the front of the eye | *At the back of the inside of the eye
exercise: What does the retina do? | *It senses light and sends messages to the brain | It pumps blood around the body | It makes the eye shine green | It bends the light into glasses
exercise: «Glasses lenses bend light so it focuses on the retina.» Why do glasses help us see? | *They bend light so the picture lands sharply on the retina | They stop the eyes from seeing colour | They keep all the light out of the eye | They make the eyes worse over time
test: «The image on the retina is upside down; the brain turns it round.» What does the brain do with the image? | It sends it down to the feet | It makes it dark | It stores it as a word | *It turns it the right way up
test: Why do cats' eyes shine in the dark? | Cats have no lens in their eyes | Cats have green paint inside their eyes | *A shiny layer behind the retina bounces light back through the eye | Cats' retinas are made of glass
exam: What is the retina? | A bone in the skull | The clear front of the eye | *The thin layer at the back of the eye that senses light | A kind of glasses lens
